concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Section 19AB"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the section, substitute: 19AB  When court must fix non-parole period  (1) Subject to subsection (3), a court must fix a single non-parole period in respect of a federal sentence or federal sentences if:  (a) a person is convicted of a federal offence, or of 2 or more federal offences at the same sitting; and  (b) the court imposes the sentence or sentences on the person; and  (c) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:  (i) any of the sentences is a federal life sentence;  (ii) the sentences, in the aggregate, exceed 3 years; and  (d) when the court imposes the sentence or sentences, the person is not already serving or subject to a federal sentence.  (2) Subject to subsection (3), a court must fix a single non-parole period in respect of all federal sentences a person is to serve or complete if:  (a) while the person is in prison and is serving or subject to a federal sentence, the court imposes a further federal sentence on the person; and  (b) the result is that the person is to serve or to complete:  (i) a federal life sentence; or  (ii) federal sentences the unserved portions of which, in the aggregate, exceed 3 years; and  (c) when the court imposes the further federal sentence, the person is not already subject to a non-parole period or recognizance release order in respect of a federal sentence. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 7  Sentencing and parole" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the section, substitute: 19AB  When court must fix non-parole period  (1) Subject to subsection (3), a court must fix a single non-parole period in respect of a federal sentence or federal sentences if:  (a) a person is convicted of a federal offence, or of 2 or more federal offences at the same sitting; and  (b) the court imposes the sentence or sentences on the person; and  (c) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:  (i) any of the sentences is a federal life sentence;  (ii) the sentences, in the aggregate, exceed 3 years; and  (d) when the court imposes the sentence or sentences, the person is not already serving or subject to a federal sentence.  (2) Subject to subsection (3), a court must fix a single non-parole period in respect of all federal sentences a person is to serve or complete if:  (a) while the person is in prison and is serving or subject to a federal sentence, the court imposes a further federal sentence on the person; and  (b) the result is that the person is to serve or to complete:  (i) a federal life sentence; or  (ii) federal sentences the unserved portions of which, in the aggregate, exceed 3 years; and  (c) when the court imposes the further federal sentence, the person is not already subject to a non-parole period or recognizance release order in respect of a federal sentence. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 7  Sentencing and parole"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "798aaed207f26fcac0d7b0f759c2fa9314b20ee5ca980bbc4d3ba42b2fc6ff82" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-10-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-10-ss-2 ;
