    cof:title "10(2) Section 19AB" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subject to subsection (3), a court must fix a single non-parole period in respect of all federal sentences a person is to serve or complete if:  (a) while the person is in prison and is serving or subject to a federal sentence, the court imposes a further federal sentence on the person; and  (b) the result is that the person is to serve or to complete:  (i) a federal life sentence; or  (ii) federal sentences the unserved portions of which, in the aggregate, exceed 3 years; and  (c) when the court imposes the further federal sentence, the person is not already subject to a non-parole period or recognizance release order in respect of a federal sentence. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 7  Sentencing and parole" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer .

