    cof:title "38(1) After section 19AP" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may, at any time before the end of:  (a) a parole period for a person for whom a parole order has been made; or  (b) a licence period for a person who is released on licence for a federal sentence; by order in writing, amend the parole order or licence by doing any or all of the following:  (c) imposing additional conditions on the parole order or licence;  (d) varying or revoking a condition of the parole order or licence specified under paragraph 19AN(1)(c) or 19AP(7)(c) or imposed under paragraph (a);  (e) if the supervision period has not ended—changing the day on which the supervision period ends. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Sentencing and parole  Schedule 7 Amendments of parole orders and licences  Part 9  No. 153, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other Measures) Act 2015  Amendments to rectify errors etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-38-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "38(2) After section 19AP"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-38-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a parole order or licence:  (a) contains an error of a technical nature; or  (b) has a defect of form; or  (c) contains an ambiguity; the Attorney-General may, at any time, by order in writing, amend the parole order or licence to rectify the error, defect or ambiguity. Note: For paragraph (a), the following are examples of errors of a technical nature: a clerical mistake, an accidental slip or omission, a material miscalculation of figures or a material mistake in the description of a person, thing or matter. When amendments take effect" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If a parole order or licence:  (a) contains an error of a technical nature; or  (b) has a defect of form; or  (c) contains an ambiguity; the Attorney-General may, at any time, by order in writing, amend the parole order or licence to rectify the error, defect or ambiguity. Note: For paragraph (a), the following are examples of errors of a technical nature: a clerical mistake, an accidental slip or omission, a material miscalculation of figures or a material mistake in the description of a person, thing or matter. When amendments take effect"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "93ca8f3764d5a9a5a10b5925fad35e4931c14b9d31cdc869fc17608d3feae7c3" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-38 ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Attorney-General may amend parole order or licence to rectify errors, defects or ambiguities." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
