concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-46 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "46 Subsection 20AB(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-46 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) A court may pass a sentence, or make an order, in respect of a person convicted before the court in a participating State or participating Territory of a federal offence, if:  (a) subsection (1AA) applies to the sentence or order; and  (b) under the law of the State or Territory, a court is empowered to pass such a sentence, or make such an order, in respect of a State or Territory offender in corresponding cases; and  (c) the first-mentioned court is:  (i) empowered as mentioned in paragraph (b); or  (ii) a federal court.  (1AA) This subsection applies to a sentence or order that is:  (a) known as any of the following:  (i) an attendance centre order or attendance order;  (ii) a community based order;  (iii) a community correction order;  (iv) a community custody order;  (v) a community service order;  (vi) a community work order;  (vii) a drug or alcohol treatment order or rehabilitation order; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 7  Sentencing and parole" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) A court may pass a sentence, or make an order, in respect of a person convicted before the court in a participating State or participating Territory of a federal offence, if:  (a) subsection (1AA) applies to the sentence or order; and  (b) under the law of the State or Territory, a court is empowered to pass such a sentence, or make such an order, in respect of a State or Territory offender in corresponding cases; and  (c) the first-mentioned court is:  (i) empowered as mentioned in paragraph (b); or  (ii) a federal court.  (1AA) This subsection applies to a sentence or order that is:  (a) known as any of the following:  (i) an attendance centre order or attendance order;  (ii) a community based order;  (iii) a community correction order;  (iv) a community custody order;  (v) a community service order;  (vi) a community work order;  (vii) a drug or alcohol treatment order or rehabilitation order; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 7  Sentencing and parole"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "34afcfdcaae911b88b3f7f3f86ff6ca38b964c91db24e1f6ce8acf1e5afa3d6b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A court may pass a sentence or make an order in respect of a person convicted before the court in a participating State or Territory of a federal offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
