concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-9-sec-20bz-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20BZ(1) Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-9-sec-20bz-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An authorised officer may disclose federal offender information to a relevant person if the officer reasonably believes that the disclosure is necessary to enable the relevant person to exercise the person’s powers, or to perform the person’s functions or duties." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An authorised officer may disclose federal offender information to a relevant person if the officer reasonably believes that the disclosure is necessary to enable the relevant person to exercise the person’s powers, or to perform the person’s functions or duties."@en ;
