concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-18 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18 Subsections 58(1), (2) and (3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-18 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute: Advice to person who referred issue under section 23  (1) The Integrity Commissioner may advise a person (or a representative nominated by the person) of the outcome of an investigation of a corruption issue raised by the person in a referral under section 23. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other Measures) Act 2015 No. 153, 2015  Manner of giving advice  (2) One way of advising the person (or the representative) is to give a copy of all or part of any report prepared under subsection 54(1) in relation to the investigation." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsections, substitute: Advice to person who referred issue under section 23  (1) The Integrity Commissioner may advise a person (or a representative nominated by the person) of the outcome of an investigation of a corruption issue raised by the person in a referral under section 23. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other Measures) Act 2015 No. 153, 2015  Manner of giving advice  (2) One way of advising the person (or the representative) is to give a copy of all or part of any report prepared under subsection 54(1) in relation to the investigation."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4f6a8b58960165aedd9abfbaaf82bae89a12523ca4a765199321393f7d7d2e7b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer ;
