concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 After section 24AB"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-12-sec-6 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: 24ABA  Examiner may direct that returnable items be returned  (1) If an examiner conducting an examination is satisfied that a returnable item produced by a person during the examination:  (a) is not required (or is no longer required) for the purposes of the ACC operation/investigation to which the examination relates; or  (b) will no longer be so required once certain conditions (the return conditions) have been met; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 12  Australian Crime Commission  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other Measures) Act 2015 No. 153, 2015  the examiner may, at or before the time the person is excused or released from further attendance at the examination, direct that the item be returned to:  (c) the person; or  (d) the owner, if the person is not entitled to possess it.  (2) The direction may specify that the return of the item is subject to any return conditions being met.  (3) Members of the staff of the ACC, or any person who has been present at the examination and is in possession of the item, must comply with the direction.  (4) The examiner or the CEO may vary or revoke the direction." ;
    skos:definition "Insert: 24ABA  Examiner may direct that returnable items be returned  (1) If an examiner conducting an examination is satisfied that a returnable item produced by a person during the examination:  (a) is not required (or is no longer required) for the purposes of the ACC operation/investigation to which the examination relates; or  (b) will no longer be so required once certain conditions (the return conditions) have been met; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153  Schedule 12  Australian Crime Commission  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other Measures) Act 2015 No. 153, 2015  the examiner may, at or before the time the person is excused or released from further attendance at the examination, direct that the item be returned to:  (c) the person; or  (d) the owner, if the person is not entitled to possess it.  (2) The direction may specify that the return of the item is subject to any return conditions being met.  (3) Members of the staff of the ACC, or any person who has been present at the examination and is in possession of the item, must comply with the direction.  (4) The examiner or the CEO may vary or revoke the direction."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d5952378f5b05098fe35b3f893ef3206ffb81abf9394bcbd7bcc22d7c43f0758" ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6-ss-3 ;
